  "provider_query": "Node.js 22.0.0 GitHub release page",
  "answer": "Relevant pages for **Node.js 22.0.0** on GitHub:\n\n1. **Official release** — [nodejs/node v22.0.0](https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases/tag/v22.0.0)  \n   Published 24 Apr 2024 by RafaelGSS and marco-ippolito (tag `v22.0.0`, commit `12fb157`, verified signature). Marked Current; LTS planned for October. Highlights: `require()` of ESM graphs, WebSocket client enabled by default, V8 12.4.254.14. Also notes watch mode stable, dropped import assertions, faster AbortSignal creation, and a higher stream `highWaterMark`. [web:0][web:8]\n\n2. **Blog source on GitHub** — [nodejs.org `v22.0.0.md`](https://github.com/nodejs/nodejs.org/blob/main/apps/site/pages/en/blog/release/v22.0.0.md)  \n   Release post source with installer/binary links under `https://nodejs.org/dist/v22.0.0/` and docs at `https://nodejs.org/docs/v22.0.0/api/`. [web:2]\n\n3. **v22 changelog** — [CHANGELOG_V22.md (main)](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/main/doc/changelogs/CHANGELOG_V22.md)  \n   Full v22 line changelog in the node repo. [web:6]\n\n4. **v22 changelog (branch)** — [CHANGELOG_V22.md (v22.x)](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/v22.x/doc/changelogs/CHANGELOG_V22.md)  \n   Same changelog on the `v22.x` branch. [web:12]\n\n5. **All node tags** — [nodejs/node tags](https://github.com/nodejs/node/tags)  \n   Tag index for the runtime repo (later v22.x LTS tags such as Jod appear here as well). [web:1]\n\n6. **Node repo overview** — [nodejs/node](https://github.com/nodejs/node)  \n   Describes Current vs LTS vs nightly builds and download layout; nightly names include a version like `v22.0.0` plus date and commit. [web:3]\n\n7. **Release commit list (same tag)** — more of the v22.0.0 notes on the same GitHub release, including semver-patch dependency bumps (npm 10.5.1, nghttp2, c-ares, zlib, simdutf, simdjson). [web:10]\n\n8. **Not the runtime** — other `v22.0.0` tags (e.g. [gibme-npm/starlink](https://github.com/gibme-npm/starlink/releases/tag/v22.0.0), [stripe/stripe-node](https://github.com/stripe/stripe-node/releases/tag/v22.0.0)) are unrelated package releases that only mention Node 22 or share the version number. [web:9][web:11]\n\nDirect release URL: https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases/tag/v22.0.0",
